#* {{quote-book|en|year=1992|title=Newsweek - Volume 120|author=|page=55|isbn=|passage=When NBC licensed his reruns to the Arts & Entertainment cable network without consulting him, he was incensed. "It was a '''rinky-dink''' deal," says a source.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|title=Since My Last Confession: A Gay Catholic Memoir|author=Scott Pomfret|page=246|isbn=1611455006|passage=I asked Father Butterballino, “Why do it at all, if you're going to do it in this '''rinky-dink''', sneaky way?” (phrased more diplomatically, of course).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2012|title=Almost Midnight: An American Story of Murder and Redemption|author=Michael W. Cuneo|page=|isbn=0307815455|passage=He'd paid a fine on that '''rinky-dink''' deal at the courthouse in Forsyth the very next day.}}
