#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|title=John Lee Johnson and the Gunslingers|author=Conn Hamlett|page=13|isbn=1458211282|passage=The loud '''rinky-dink''' music and the wafting blue cigar smoke made the scene a dime novel cover.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2017|title=Experiencing Film Music: A Listener's Companion|author=Kenneth LaFave|page=32|isbn=144225842X|passage=But Humphrey Bogart's Philip Marlowe has no sax sound tagging along behind him, and when love interest Lauren Bacall makes her entrance at a swanky nightspot, a '''rinky-dink''' piano accompanies her sway; there's not a sax in sight (or sound).}}

